[{:db/id -1, :adr/id "adr-2606101130", :adr/title "ADR-2606101130: Session-Close — basic-infrastructure robotics 3-layer wave + kami-genesis physics bridge", :adr/status "accepted", :adr/doc_type "adr", :adr/source-format "edn", :adr/body "\n# ADR-2606101130: Session-Close — basic-infrastructure robotics 3-layer wave + kami-genesis physics bridge\n\n**Date**: 2026-06-10\n**Status**: ACCEPTED (process record)\n**Deciders**: Jun Kawasaki\n\n# Context\n\nThe session opened with the audit question *「電気水道ガス通信などの基本インフラを運営設計する\nrobotics の設計はどれぐらいできている?」* and the directive *「実際に稼働する前提まで進めてほしい」*\n(all four domains, full 3-layer depth). The audit found wide charter/ADR/cell scaffolding but\nalmost no runnable robotics: every domain `cell.py .solve()` raised `RuntimeError`; the open-ot\nIEC 61499 Rust WASM PLC existed (8 BFBs) but connected to nothing; kuni-umi's\n`commissioning/cell.py` raised `NotImplementedError` at the open-ot seam; the kami-engine physics\nsubmodule was not checked out; the only real control code anywhere was noroshi's fibre aligner.\n\n# What was done (two waves)\n\n## Wave 1 — 3-layer operational substrate + 4 verticals (PR #1531, MERGED → ADR-2606091800)\n\nOne shared substrate at `20-actors/kuni-umi/robotics/` (stdlib-only, deterministic,\n`:representative`): **plant** (swing-eqn microgrid + first-order plants — the kami-genesis\nstand-in) + **control** (PID anti-windup / Droop / DroopPI / `simulate()` — the open-ot\nfield-tier twin) + **kinematics** (PlanarArm FK / analytic IK / joint trajectories) +\n**safety** (closed-world civilian allowlist N1 · no-server-key G15/G7 · witness quorum ≥2 G8 ·\nhuman-proximity SafetyEnvelope) + **commissioning** (the runnable kuni-umi→open-ot handoff;\nthe `NotImplementedError` seam now delegates to it, live XRPC still `deps.sdk`-gated).\n\nReplicated as four end-to-end verticals, each with its safety crux structurally enforced:\n**hikari 電気** (droop+PI restores 50 Hz after a load step; windowed ROCOF anti-islanding guard;\nOtete panel-install reach/IK/envelope) · **mizuho 水道** (reservoir PI; chlorination residual\nhard-clamped ≤ 4.0 mg/L by doser-clamp + plant-ceiling defence-in-depth; G6 fluoride requires\nper-member consent; G3 community-scale cap) · **kamado ガス/精製** (PI purge drives H₂S/benzene\nbelow entry limits; robot entry into an un-purged zone raises `SafetyError` before any motion\nplanning; G9 displacement cohort carried on every plan) · **noroshi 通信** (fibre lay→align→splice\nreusing the existing Hooke-Jeeves aligner + IEC 60825 gate; fusion splice ≤ 0.10 dB).\n\n## Wave 2 — kami-genesis physics bridge (PR #1538)\n\nThe submodule `40-engine/kami-engine` was populated for the first time in this line of work, and\nthe \"swap is mechanical\" promise of ADR-2606091800 was converted from claim to proof:\n`kami-bridge/` (a standalone Rust crate path-depending on the submodule, **no submodule edits**)\nloads a 2-link parity URDF with the exact `PlanarArm((1.2, 1.0))` geometry plus the real\n`giemon_arm6` 6-DOF fixture via `kami_articulated::parse_urdf` → `Articulation3dConfig`\n(Featherstone RNEA+CRBA), and emits a deterministic golden FK/IK trace\n(`golden/kami_fk_ik_trace.json`, committed — the parity suite runs without Rust).\n`test_kami_parity.py` (+8 tests) asserts: FK parity on the full 56-sample grid (f32 tolerance);\nRust DLS-IK solutions land on target under **Python** FK; Python analytic `ik2` solves every\nreachable golden target including one the iterative DLS stalls on (recorded asymmetry);\ngiemon_arm6 is 6-DOF with sane limits, FK inside the workspace bound, position-IK < 1 mm.\n\n## Registrations (this ADR's wave)\n\ndeps.toml gains `[[adrs]]` entries for ADR-2606091800 and this session-close, and a `[[modules]]`\nentry for `20-actors/kuni-umi/robotics`. CLAUDE.md status row updated to the post-bridge state.\n\n# Consequences\n\n- Test totals: **383 green** across substrate (36 incl. 8 parity) + hikari 25 + mizuho 26 +\n  kamado 52 + noroshi 244.\n- Constitutional invariants untouched and strengthened in code: no live actuation\n  (every `cell.py .solve()` stays Council-gated; `server_held_key=False` + `dry_run=True` on every\n  record); open-ot remains the hard-RT SSoT under a certified IEC 61508/61511 PLC; Murakumo-only\n  inference unaffected (the loops are deterministic).\n- Honest limits: plants are lumped-parameter `:representative` models with test-tuned gains, not\n  commissioning-grade physics; the parity proof covers the planar FK/IK contract + giemon_arm6\n  readiness, not contact/dynamics.\n\n# Follow-ups (tracked, gated)\n\n1. **R1 device-in-the-loop** per actor — blocked on each actor's existing R1 trigger list\n   (Council Lv6+ ratify, domain engineer on advisory, LANDS parcel, sourcing-audit frameworks).\n2. **Full 6-DOF swap** — replace the planar install-arm model with giemon_arm6 task sims inside\n   the kami-engine submodule (its own repo/PR lane), now de-risked by the committed golden trace.\n3. **open-ot acceptance-rig integration** — run the Rust BFBs (DROOP_P_F / ANTI_ISLANDING_ROCOF)\n   under the wasmtime gate-a rig against the same plant scenarios the Python twin passes.\n\n# Alternatives Considered\n\nCovered in ADR-2606091800 (check out the submodule first / port BFBs to Python / un-gate\n`.solve()` — all rejected there; this record adds nothing new).\n\n# References\n\n- ADR-2606091800 — the substance (3-layer substrate + 4 verticals)\n- PR #1531 (merged 2026-06-10 JST) · PR #1538 (the bridge, this branch)\n- `20-actors/kuni-umi/robotics/` · `20-actors/{hikari,mizuho,kamado,noroshi}/methods|cells/`\n- `60-apps/etzhayyim-project-open-ot/` · `40-engine/kami-engine` @ 8e60f9a (read-only)\n", :adr/path "90-docs/adr/2606101130-session-close-infra-robotics-3layer-and-kami-physics-bridge.edn", :adr/source-repo "root", :adr/topic "session-close-infra-robotics-3layer-kami-physics-bridge", :adr/last_verified "2026-06-10", :adr/date "2026-06-10", :adr/authoritative true, :adr/related ["adr-2606091800-infra-robotics-3layer-operational-substrate" "adr-2605201400 (kuni-umi planetary-infra fleet)"], :adr/authoritative_for ["session-close summary of the infra-robotics 3-layer + kami-physics-bridge wave (2026-06-09 … 06-10)" "deps.toml registration of ADR-2606091800 + the kuni-umi/robotics module"]}]
